# Code Style (Cross-Cutting)

## Biome Configuration

Biome handles JS/TS/JSON/CSS formatting and linting. Configured in root `biome.json`.

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Indent | 2 spaces |
| Line width | 120 characters |
| Line ending | LF |
| Quote style | Single quotes (JS/TS), double quotes (CSS/SCSS) |
| JSX quote style | Double quotes |
| Trailing commas | ES5 |
| Semicolons | Always |
| Arrow parentheses | Always |
| Bracket spacing | `true` |
| Bracket same line | `false` |

### Key Lint Rules

- **`noConsole`**: Error — only `console.warn` and `console.error` allowed
- **Import organization**: Auto-sorted by Biome
- Console is allowed in `scripts/`, `bin/`, build configs, and test files

### Prettier

Only for MD/MDX files. Not for JS/TS — Biome handles that.

## TypeScript Conventions

- TypeScript ~6.0 with strict mode
- Use `type` imports where applicable
- `AllowedTypes` for prop validation in Stencil components
- `PropTypes<typeof Component>` pattern for type-safe prop definitions
- `BreakpointCustomizable<T>` for responsive prop values
- `SelectedAriaAttributes<A>` for ARIA prop types

## Component Naming

| Context | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Web component tag | `p-` prefix, kebab-case | `p-button`, `p-input-text` |
| Stencil class | PascalCase matching tag | `Button`, `InputText` |
| React wrapper | `P` prefix + PascalCase | `PButton`, `PInputText` |
| Angular wrapper | Same as React | `PButton`, `PInputText` |
| Vue wrapper file | PascalCase + `Wrapper` | `ButtonWrapper.vue`, `InputTextWrapper.vue` |

## Prop Naming Conventions

- **Feature-based**, not action-based: `compact` not `enableCompact`
- **Avoid action/state verbs**: `show`, `hide`, `enable`, `disable`
- **Boolean props**: Default to `false`, use positive naming (`disabled` not `notEnabled`)

| Incorrect | Correct |
|-----------|---------|
| `showPasswordToggle` | `toggle` |
| `enableDarkMode` | `mode` |
| `isActive` | `active` |
| `hideBorder` | `border` or `borderVisible` |
| `disableAnimation` | `animation` |

## File Naming

- Component files: `{component-name}.tsx` (kebab-case)
- Style files: `{component-name}-styles.ts`
- Utility files: `{component-name}-utils.ts`
- Test files: `{component-name}.spec.ts`, `{component-name}-styles.spec.ts`
- React wrappers: `{component}.wrapper.tsx`
- Angular wrappers: `{component}.wrapper.ts`
- Vue wrappers: `{Component}Wrapper.vue` (PascalCase)

## JSS Style Object Conventions

```ts
export const getComponentCss = (variant: Variant, isDisabled: boolean): string => {
  return getCss({
    root: {
      transition: getTransition('opacity'),
      ...(isDisabled && {
        ...getDisabledBaseStyles(),
      }),
    },
    label: {
      // styles
    },
    icon: {
      // styles
    },
  });
};
```

- Class names as object keys: `root`, `label`, `icon`, `spinner`, `counter`
- Conditional styles via spread: `...(condition && { /* styles */ })`
- Style composition via `mergeDeep(baseStyles, overrideStyles)`
- Never hardcode token values — import from `../../styles/css-variables`

## CSS Variable Naming

| Prefix | Scope | JSDoc Required | Example |
|--------|-------|----------------|---------|
| `--p-*` | Global design tokens | No | `--p-color-primary` |
| `--p-<component>-*` | Public writable API | Yes | `--p-flyout-width` |
| `--ref-p-<component>-*` | Public read-only API | Yes | `--ref-p-flyout-pt` |
| `--_p-<component>-{a,b,c}` | Internal | No | `--_p-button-a` |

Internal variables use single-letter suffixes to keep them terse and signal "do not depend on this."

## Import Conventions

- Relative imports within packages
- `@porsche-design-system/*` scoped imports across packages
- Barrel exports via `index.ts`
- Biome auto-sorts imports — don't fight it

## Files That Must Not Be Edited

- `dist/` directories — generated build output
- `src/lib/` in `shared` and `component-meta` — generated during build
- `*.props.md` — auto-generated prop documentation
- `package-lock.json` — run `npm install` to regenerate
- Generated wrapper files in `components-react`, `components-angular`, `components-vue`
